  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving community resilience by Strengthening Disease Outbreak Prevention and response with a One Health approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP proposes to develop a comprehensive One Health framework including implementationof effective Community Outreach programme, developing a robust communication strategy plan and piloting the predictive disease models for early detection and risk mapping of zoonotic diseases in the districts, establish a digital platform to implement a One Health collaborative network for forewarning and mitigating risk of future pandemics involving key stakeholders from veterinary, public health, and environmental sectors. The key activities are as follows:BRIEF DESCRIPTION1 Pilot Integrated digital platformslike AVIN, Zoo-WIN, dashboard analytics for disease outbreak predictionsin Tamil Nadu and Bihar2. Pilot community outreach and Disease prediction models for AES In Bihar3. Development of Communication Strategy document for DAHD</narrative>
  </description>
